## Lore

The phoenixi, also called fire birds and Children of the Phoenix, are large
humanoids with the head of a stork or crane, a body covered in tiny red and
gold feathers, and flaming red wings. Two long golden crest feathers rise to
signal danger and readiness to fight. Legend makes them the offspring of
Bennu the Phoenix, whom they call their All-mother, though they are more
likely creatures of magic from another dimension, kin to the spirits of light
or fire elementals.

Curious and fond of life, the phoenixi long ago learned the secrets of ley
lines and dimensional travel and left their homeworld to wander the Megaverse
as explorers. Most practise non-involvement, staying out of local politics and
trouble, which can make them seem cold to outsiders. Many cannot stay entirely
impartial and will warn, mediate or heal; some abandon neutrality altogether,
take sides and even adopt a world as home for centuries. A true friend is to a
phoenixi one of life''s greatest gifts, and they are fiercely loyal to the few
they have.

In the wars of the Egyptian gods they try to remain neutral, acting as
heralds and mediators, and those who do take part usually join Bennu''s side
and prefer non-combat roles, though some have become renowned warriors.

## GM Notes

Phoenixi explorers travel alone, in pairs or in groups of 1D4+2. They prefer
forests and wild places where they can fly; small groups live in Africa, the
Phoenix Empire, India and Asia. Scholars guess there are only about a million
of them in the cosmos. Evil gods and bio-wizards covet their regeneration.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'phoenixi');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'phoenixi';

